    "rich_text_3Y6zYY": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_GdMYJe": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>Find Your Best Prescription Scuba Mask</strong>",
            "set_h1": false,
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_wHAUN9": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choosing the right new prescription swim mask starts with understanding your current prescription and underwater vision needs. Most divers use their Sphere values as a starting point, while some may also require Cylinder correction for astigmatism. Depending on the mask model, you can choose from premade RX lenses, drop-in corrective lenses, or custom prescription dive masks based on a combined refractive equivalent. This uses your Sphere and your Cylinder reading to give the best vision under water.<br/><br/></p><p>For snorkeling, scuba diving, and recreational swim use, a well-fitted prescription mask improves clarity, comfort, and overall field of vision underwater. Tempered glass lenses, adjustable straps, and soft silicone skirts help create an extremely comfortable fit, while quality optics provide clear vision for both casual snorkelers and experienced divers.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_GdMYJe",
        "text_wHAUN9"
      ],
